The attached image (Fig. 11) illustrates the residual inflammation at injection sites two weeks post-injection with either aluminum hydroxide (AH) adjuvant (left panel) or Nano-11 (right panel). The left panel, representing AH, shows extensive granulomatous inflammation (indicated by asterisks), characterized by dense cellular infiltration within the skeletal muscle. In contrast, the right panel, representing Nano-11, exhibits significantly less inflammation (asterisk) with relatively few macrophages arranged in slender cords. This demonstrates that Nano-11 induces a more transient and rapidly resolving inflammatory response compared to the persistent granulomatous inflammation caused by AH.